        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "84deb25a-0637-3e32-af06-c13465f83680",
                "word": "chasse-café",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e70333e-f5d5-3127-a902-2e07c407a23f",
                        "entry_id": "84deb25a-0637-3e32-af06-c13465f83680",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Spiritueux que l’on sert après le café, à la fin d’un repas."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "16c08317-f6fa-460c-84a1-d7f541b19533",
                                "sense_id": "2e70333e-f5d5-3127-a902-2e07c407a23f",
                                "text": "La musique cessa de jouer quand les dames quittèrent la salle à manger ; nous nous rapprochâmes alors les uns des autres , et la conversation devint plus animée. Quand les vins commencèrent à circuler plus lentement, on apporta le café et le chasse-café."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fe1b34e-27e5-4007-a747-0d884f610b5a",
                                "sense_id": "2e70333e-f5d5-3127-a902-2e07c407a23f",
                                "text": "Sir Louis demanda alors à Janete de lui apporter un chasse-café.\n« Du café autant que vous en voudrez, lui répondit-elle, mais sans eau-de-vie. »"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e8bd9a57-05ae-4dac-abde-791fa39f5677",
                        "source_entry_id": "84deb25a-0637-3e32-af06-c13465f83680",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e70333e-f5d5-3127-a902-2e07c407a23f",
                        "target_lang_word": "chasse-café",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chasse-café",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                        "entry_id": "6328a5c1-edfc-3b9f-a8ea-4ce2ac577be7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small serving of spirits taken to remove the taste of coffee, tobacco, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba850007-31af-4260-8882-a626f1931158",
                                                "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                                "text": "\"[…] And here comes tea and coffee—may as well have some, I suppose it will be all the same price. And what's this?\" eyeing a lot of liqueur glasses full of eau de vie. \"Chasse café, Monsieur,\" said the garçon. \"Chasse cafe—chasse cafe—what's that? Oh, I twig—what we call 'shove in the mouth' at the Free-and-Easy.—Yes, certainly, give me a glass.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e615a3ec-7782-4b07-a213-4043e85b8fd9",
                                                "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                                "text": "The business of the drama is now over, and by way of epilogue, you toss off a demi-tasse of café noir, with its accompanying petit verre de liqueur, which has been appositely termed chasse-café, from the peculiar rapidity it usually exhibits in following that aromatic beverage. […] Such are the details of a Parsian dinner; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e601bce5-6a96-4596-ac94-66ccc3e507ed",
                                                "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                                "text": "The former will have devoted himself to you for the first half-score hours, have promenaded, dined à la carte, and chasse café’d with you, seen you to your hotel with bows, promises, and ravishing language, and then—have forgotten you for ever."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b915039-893d-4c77-abb2-3ac8d480a290",
                                                "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                                "text": "The dinner was in the best French manner—choice fruit, and wines of the greatest variety and richness; melon, with boiled beef as usual; coffee after dinner, without cream, and a small glass of liqueur called chasse-café, after it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8983f11-93b2-4a26-b5a4-c632644388bf",
                                                "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                                "text": "Sir Louis began by ordering the woman to bring him chasse-café. She offered him coffee, as much as he would; but no chasse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70ef2331-a5f3-4c00-82d3-fd963530075b",
                                                "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                                "text": "I could not understand why they gave us unlimited light claret for dinner, with Madeira and champagne, with any number of chasse cafés, all included in the passage-money, whilst any one calling for a modest glass of ale had to pay extra, and pretty handsomely, for the same."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6733f80a-0189-416d-b484-a59ca62114d4",
                                                "sense_id": "ba9d7f33-bad1-398f-9a6d-98454ebe3966",
                                                "text": "At the concert (which was at three) I found [Anton] Rubinstein who is here visiting his wife for Christmas. We dined together (at the Grand Hôtel de Russie, Babuino). As a chasse-café I banged out for him my arrangement of the Tic-tac Tarantelle by [Alexander] Dargomizhsky."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
